 # Change record
+
+## V7.3, 5 October 2026
+
+Ren asked that the theory provide ways for institutions to move toward durable correction and authorized continued work toward a justified V7.3. All current workspace changes were checkpointed at `deabb7c` before development; V7.2 is preserved. This entry records the addition; RELEASE-REVIEW gives the completed readiness assessment.
+
+### Constructive development
+
+Section 11.6 distinguishes direction of improvement, adoption, a protected transition and continuing implementation. The reachability table now distinguishes voluntary coordination from legitimate binding correction: unanimous preference is not a general requirement. S17 adds `reformpath`, one conditional finite construction into S16's protected region from specified imperfect states. It accounts for construction delay, temporary correction, structural change, sufficient resource and host reserve, and the lower continuing maintenance after temporary intervention ends. Its implementation assumptions remain explicit. Standard reach-and-remain control methodology is credited; no general mathematical-priority claim is made.
+
+X10 adds a worked procurement illustration beginning with an existing programme's powers and constraints. Evidence, authorization, execution, service fallback, succession and valid appeals are assessed together. Test N adds a proposed and unrun bounded comparison with a resources-matched alternative and failed adoption included. The example supplies neither empirical calibration nor powers over unenrolled frontier developers.
+
+### Evidence, preservation and verification
+
+EV20 records the diagnostic institutional-design and reach-and-remain literature, with primary-source retrieval scope. CLAIMS §12 records provenance while §§8–11 retain the previous record. The bilingual opening and main conclusion distinguish the new reduced path from the still-open political implementation and empirical diagnosis.
+
+The edition uses `assemble_v73.py`, `refs_v73.py`, `xref_v73.py`, `checks_v73.py` and `verification/audit_v73.py`. New block PT checks the transition and adverse cases. The complete default run passed 249 counted checks across 46 blocks with zero failures. Preservation, assembly and cross-reference checks passed; the three fresh bounded reviews and their resolved findings are recorded in RELEASE-REVIEW. The institutional pilot is unrun, and this revision does not publish or externally distribute the work.
 
